  year      = {1995},
  pages     = {461-465},
  publisher = {ACM Press},
  abstract  = {In this paper we present NEFCLASS, a neuro-fuzzy system for the classification of data. This approach is based on our generic model of a fuzzy perceptron which can be used to derive fuzzy neural networks or neural fuzzy systems for specific domains. The presented model derives fuzzy rules from data to classify patterns into a number of (crisp) classes. NEFCLASS uses a supervised learning algorithm based on fuzzy error backpropagation that is used in other derivations of the fuzzy perceptron.},
